Built stdlib-only compress.py with both requested CLI modes, using inferred numeric-column patterns, dictionary encoding, and LZMA, plus a lossless fallback. Verified the restored corpus byte-for-byte with cmp: 313,972 bytes compress to 4,757 bytes, a 98.4849% size reduction, beating default zlib’s 35,399 bytes. Registered python3 assay.py to validate the round trip and print the percentage reduction.